export abstract anchor FactoryDelivery:
    unmergedPrerequisites:
        Dependent work may start from a finished prerequisite branch before
        integration once that prerequisite passes its required checks and
        higher-level completion assessment. Track the exact prerequisite
        version used by the dependent work. If the prerequisite changes or is
        rejected, delegate reconciliation before treating the dependent result
        as complete. Merging alone need not block useful dependent work.
    integrationChecks:
        Integration includes checking that concurrent changes work together
        before accepting their merge, even when each change passed separately.
        Combine the changes and run the relevant project-defined checks on
        that combined result. Ordinary code runs the checks; delegate conflicts
        and failures requiring judgment to agents. This requirement does not
        prescribe one universal test suite across projects.
    completion:
        Agents and their generated plans and instructions determine completion
        criteria, testing, and reviews, ultimately driven by the prompt,
        specification, or both. The factory does not independently impose
        universal testing or review gates. Desired product outcomes belong to
        individual orders rather than to a fixed category of factory output.
    completionAssessment:
        An implementation agent reports a step done. A different higher-level
        agent in a different session assesses the claim against the brief and
        expected result without taking over the work.
        Order completion requires all required steps completed, approved
        deferred steps recorded, integration and delivery outcomes recorded, and
        an independent assessment. The assessor is not an implementer of any
        required step and did not author criteria after implementation. Criteria
        are frozen before implementation or approved above the implementer. One
        order assessor accepts step assessments. If the top tier implemented,
        the engineer or a fresh independent reviewer with defined authority
        assesses.
        Completion evidence is a manifest of result versions, checks, artifacts,
        diff identity, assessor identity, and delivery receipts. A change before
        completion forces revalidation. After completion the evidence is frozen
        and changes create a successor order.
    deferral:
        Deferred steps are proposed by planning and approved by the engineer
        with a recorded reason and a configured cap. All value-bearing steps
        cannot be deferred. Deferred work becomes a linked follow-up order at
        completion and stays visible in status.
    delivery:
        Delivery is a tracked operation with outcomes succeeded, partial,
        failed, or unnecessary, an idempotency key per target, per-target
        receipts, and bounded retries. Target records, integration, unresolved
        effects, and receipts follow FactoryIntegration. Partial delivery
        records the remainder and creates follow-up work. Delivery failure
        leaves the order active or blocked, never completed. Corrections after completion use successor
        orders and record the prior external state.
    successorOrders:
        A completed order is immutable. Reopening creates a successor order with
        a link and reason; there is no reopen operation. Post-completion
        invalidation and corrections use successor orders.
    implementationCompletionHandoff:
        Completion checking is part of the delegated workflow. When an
        implementation agent reports done, a higher-level agent checks what
        that claim means against the assigned work and its expected result.
        Keep this assessment focused; the higher-level agent should not take
        on substantial implementation or investigation itself. Delegate
        further investigation or corrections as needed. This handoff does not
        prescribe a universal test suite or full review pass for every step.
    supportingRoles:
        Different agents also handle merging, testing, and multiple levels of
        review. Completion assessment and integration responsibilities follow
        the defined handoff and integration requirements; other detailed
        responsibilities remain open.
    reviewApproach:
        When a workflow includes review, use a fresh reviewer with a focused
        brief containing the requirements, relevant changes, and checks to run.
        The reviewer forms an initial assessment before consulting the
        implementer's explanation, then may use that explanation to resolve
        specific questions. Match review depth to the work's difficulty and
        risk, reserving full blind review for difficult or high-risk work and
        lighter review for routine changes. This does not impose a universal
        review gate on every order.
    workspaceIsolation:
        Git worktrees are the mechanism for isolating concurrent implementation
        work. Every step that writes files gets its own worktree and branch.
        Read-only and review steps use the artifact under review rather than a
        separate worktree. Track the exact prerequisite version each result
        used. Worktrees whose work is finished are always cleaned up after any
        required outputs are integrated or preserved. Cleanup requires a
        committed preservation record with artifact identifiers, a pinned commit
        or durable diff bundle and hash, untracked files, and the evidence
        manifest. Cleanup never discards unfinished or unmerged work; cancelled
        unmerged work is retained until the engineer closes it or a successor
        supersedes it.
